"table, and a search hit or a link to a field in the fields view."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:527
msgid ""
"Cachemire reconnects to the connection it was closed on, with its tabs and "
"open folders. An AWS connection signs in again first, in the browser if its "
"session has expired."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:528
msgid ""
"Each time Cachemire starts, it looks for a newer version on the channel "
"picked in About (the i button of the title bar), and opens it when there is "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:529
msgid ""
"The global search lets Redis filter the data itself, so far less of it "
"travels. It uses the server's CPU while it runs, needs permission to run "
"scripts, and goes back to the normal search if the server refuses."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:530
msgid ""
"The active profile logs in to the SSH tunnels that have no username of their "
"own. A connection that fills in its own username and password uses those "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: crates/cachemire/ui/components/settings.slint:531
msgid ""
"An SSH server whose host key isn't in the app's list or in ~/.ssh/"
"known_hosts is normally shown with its fingerprint for you to trust. Turn "
"this on to trust and remember it without asking; a key that changes is "
"always refused."
msgstr ""

